<title>HUNGARY: HUNGARY HOUSEHOLD SAVINGS GROW HUF 46.7 BLN IN OCT.</title>
<headline>HUNGARY HOUSEHOLD SAVINGS GROW HUF 46.7 BLN IN OCT.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Net household savings rose 46.7</p>
<p>billion forints in October to 2,279.2 billion forints, the</p>
<p>National Bank of Hungary said on Friday.</p>
<p>    (in billion forints) Oct 96	Sept 96    Oct 95</p>
<p> Forint savings	   2,153.8	2,110.2    1,666.9</p>
<p> Foreign currency	   473.8	  470.6	422.4</p>
<p> Total savings	    2,627.6	2,580.8    2,089.3</p>
<p> Total loans		  348.4	  348.3	372.3</p>
<p> Net household savings  2,279.2	2,232.5    1,717.0</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are not inflation adjusted. This year's</p>
<p>figures are preliminary. The consumer price inflation was 21</p>
<p>percent year-on-year in October.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom(36 1) 327-4040</p>
</text>
